"20260721171428349975_e17e939b", "text": "This Academia.edu page presents a 2020 paper by Andreas Vlachopoulos titled \"The Ring of Nestor and the quest for authenticity,\" published in F. Blakolmer (ed.), Current Approaches and New Perspectives in Aegean Iconography, Aegis 18 (2020), pp. 223-252. The
abstract says the paper reviews research on the so-called Ring of Nestor (CMS VI, no. 277), argues for its authenticity, and uses that case to discuss other Creto-Mycenaean gold rings that were once considered fakes. It also says the revision is supported by recent finds and by closer study of the 
techniques and craftsmanship of these Late Bronze Age signet rings. The abstract further proposes that the ring's main pictorial unit is a scorpion, interpreted as a major apotropaic symbol in Bronze Age Aegean iconography that kills the \"Minoan Dragon\" and provides an interpretation of the ring's 
