reidentify the key pictorial element as a scorpion, described as a major apotropaic symbol in Bronze Age Aegean iconography that "kills" the Minoan dragon of the ring, and present this reading as a new interpretation of the ring’s iconography.[6] Within the limited set of sources available here, the 
