forgery, and that new technical observations and manufacturing details are presented as aligning the ring with known Minoan–Mycenaean artifacts.[4] An abstract in A. G. Vlachopoulos’s chapter "The Ring of Nestor and the quest for authenticity" describes many years of research on the ring (catalogued 
