craftsmanship as reinforcing the reassessment of the Ring of Nestor’s authenticity within this timeframe.[6] A non‑scholarly image caption labels the Ring of Nestor as belonging to the Late Minoan I period, with a date range of circa 1700–1450 BCE, and describes it as a "Minoan Kakovatos signet ring" 
